    {"key":"reddit-hdd-deal-watch","name":"astra-reddit-hdd-deal-watch","schedule":"every 1h","prompt":"Use only the injected candidate JSON plus current web evidence from each candidate URL. If there are no candidates or collection failed, respond with only [SILENT]. Alert only for used or refurbished SATA HDDs in the US that are still available and either ship or are pickup-only in Texas. Hard per-drive limits: 4TB $40, 8TB $100, 12TB $130, 16TB $130; reject all prices above those ceilings, SSD/NVMe, whole servers, ambiguous prices, sold/pending items, and out-of-state pickup-only listings. Return one concise message under 1,500 characters only when at least one listing survives. Start with <@{{ hermes_automation_owner_user_id }}> **HDD Deal Alert** and give capacity, per-drive price, shipping or Texas pickup, and a link wrapped in angle brackets. Do not include research notes or rejected candidates.","deliver":"discord:{{ hermes_automation_logs_channel_id }}","script":"hermes-reddit-hdd-deals.py","noAgent":false,"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai-codex","enabledToolsets":["web"],"workdir":"{{ hermes_native_update_profile_home }}"},
    {"key":"daily-summary","name":"astra-daily-summary","schedule":"8 7 * * *","prompt":"Run the daily-summary-thread skill against the freshly injected Daily Summary artifact. Preserve the complete OpenClaw compose, freshness, duplicate, sequential-thread-delivery, and private continuity contract. The Hermes cron delivery target is the static Daily Summary thread; produce the complete post as the final response and do not call a send tool. If the source is unavailable or no post is due, respond with exactly [SILENT].","deliver":"discord:{{ hermes_automation_logs_channel_id }}","script":"hermes-daily-summary-input.py","noAgent":false,"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai-codex","skills":["daily-summary-thread"],"enabledToolsets":["terminal","file","discord","discord_parity"],"continuity":true,"workdir":"{{ hermes_native_update_profile_home }}"},
    {"key":"fortnite-progress","name":"astra-fortnite-progress","schedule":"50 6 * * *","prompt":"Use only the injected Fortnite progress JSON and the Fortnite Tracker skill. If STATUS is unavailable, status is not ok, or no previous snapshot exists, respond with exactly [SILENT]. Otherwise reproduce the legacy OpenClaw Fortnite progress report every day, including valid zero-activity days. If command.normalize.discordMessage is non-empty, output that message verbatim; it is the authoritative legacy renderer output. If it is empty, reconstruct the same contract: start with 🎮 **Fortnite progress:** and the overall previous-snapshot delta (matches, kills, deaths when present, wins, and minutes); include **Ranked:** with each current ranked mode's named rank and promotion/placement; include active mode breakdowns; include **7-day rolling:** overall matches, kills, wins, and K/M or K/D only when supported; include **Battle Pass:** level and progress; include milestones if present; then one short evidence-based performance read. When current rankedProgression is unavailable, include this explicitly dated historical fallback instead of dropping ranked status: last imported observation at 2026-08-19T11:40:36Z was Ranked Reload Build Diamond 3 (46% promotion) and Ranked Battle Royale Platinum 3 (8% promotion). Label it as last observed and say movement after that timestamp is unverified; never call it current or unchanged. Keep ranked BR, ranked Reload, unranked BR, Reload, and LTM separate. Never infer deaths or K/D when the source omits deaths. For a valid zero-activity day, explicitly report no new activity and preserve the supported ranked, 7-day, and Battle Pass sections; never return [SILENT] merely because deltas are zero. Do not output raw JSON or implementation notes.","deliver":"discord:{{ hermes_automation_logs_channel_id }}","script":"hermes-fortnite-progress-input.py","noAgent":false,"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai-codex","skills":["fortnite-tracker"],"enabledToolsets":["safe"],"workdir":"{{ hermes_native_update_profile_home }}"},
    {"key":"weekly-social-seeds","name":"astra-weekly-social-seeds","schedule":"0 9 * * 0","prompt":"Create at most three concise social-media idea seeds from durable non-sensitive memory and current web evidence. Reject private, medical, financial, credential, interpersonal, infrastructure-identifying, stale, repetitive, or weak material. Verify any current-status claim. Write idea seeds, not finished posts, and include one short reason each is worth developing. If nothing is safe and useful, respond with only [SILENT]. Do not expose research notes or internal reasoning.","deliver":"discord:{{ hermes_automation_social_channel_id }}","script":null,"noAgent":false,"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai-codex","enabledToolsets":["web","memory"],"workdir":"{{ hermes_native_update_profile_home }}"},
    {"key":"operational-heartbeat","name":"astra-operational-heartbeat","schedule":"every 30m","prompt":"Run the operational-heartbeat skill now. For this scheduled invocation, your final response must be exactly [SILENT] and nothing else in every case. Send any verified actionable finding only through the native Discord tool before that final response; if delivery fails, preserve the obligation in native state and still return exactly [SILENT]. Execute only due lanes, preserve per-check schedule and alert-fingerprint state, and use native Hermes runtime signals. This is unattended: never request approval, call execute_code, create or run an ad-hoc or /tmp verification script, or narrate successful internal verification. Those restrictions are normal constraints, not a verification block, lane, or alert and must never be explained in the final response. Never mention changed files, patches, syntax, or test status unless the workspace-hygiene lane is due and an exact required probe produced actionable evidence, and send any such actionable notice through Discord rather than local output. Use only existing native tools and reviewed helpers.","deliver":"local","script":null,"noAgent":false,"skills":["operational-heartbeat"],"enabledToolsets":["safe","memory","terminal","file","web","discord","discord_admin","discord_parity","agent_docker","host_admin"],"workdir":"{{ hermes_native_update_profile_home }}"},
